<http://data.silknow.org/event/47d034a3-7753-351f-9f8a-78c1abb57f5e>
        a                              ecrm:E8_Acquisition ;
        rdfs:comment                   "A label originally attached to this dress states \"Wedding dress (subsequently dyed) of Agnes E Hubbersty married N P Wood in 1848 - Red satin\".\n\nA search online revealed that the bride came from Wirksworth. The parish records as well as memorials in the parish church of Wirksworth (in Derby) between 1600-1900 have been made available online, and reveal that Agnes Eleanor Hubbersty (15 May 1812-December 8 1892) married Nicholas Price Wood, a banker and solicitor. She was the daughter of the Reverend Nathan Hubbersty BD (1767-1828) , formerly headmaster of Wirksworth grammar school, and Mary Dorothy Hubbersty (née Tomlinson) (1777-1852).\n\nFurther research uncovered that Nicholas Price Wood was born 19 Feb 1810 at Brownhills, and died at Wirksworth Hall on 10 July 1868. It also revealed that he and Agnes were married on 27 April 1843 (rather than 1848) at Darley, North Yorkshire.\n\nThe dress does not appear to have been re-dyed, so was possibly always red."@en ;
        ecrm:P14_carried_out_by        <http://data.silknow.org/actor/1d756d07-dea6-3634-9059-a00d18ccb81b> ;
        ecrm:P22_transferred_title_to  <http://data.silknow.org/actor/f0577f91-f887-3019-bf88-f9e5ba019390> ;
        ecrm:P23_transferred_title_from
                "Given by Miss W.D. Wood" ;
        ecrm:P24_transferred_title_of  <http://data.silknow.org/object/73d14723-c8d1-3670-a398-0abe53924beb> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "A label originally attached to this dress states \"Wedding dress (subsequently dyed) of Agnes E Hubbersty married N P Wood in 1848 - Red satin\".\n\nA search online revealed that the bride came from Wirksworth. The parish records as well as memorials in the parish church of Wirksworth (in Derby) between 1600-1900 have been made available online, and reveal that Agnes Eleanor Hubbersty (15 May 1812-December 8 1892) married Nicholas Price Wood, a banker and solicitor. She was the daughter of the Reverend Nathan Hubbersty BD (1767-1828) , formerly headmaster of Wirksworth grammar school, and Mary Dorothy Hubbersty (née Tomlinson) (1777-1852).\n\nFurther research uncovered that Nicholas Price Wood was born 19 Feb 1810 at Brownhills, and died at Wirksworth Hall on 10 July 1868. It also revealed that he and Agnes were married on 27 April 1843 (rather than 1848) at Darley, North Yorkshire.\n\nThe dress does not appear to have been re-dyed, so was possibly always red."@en .
